  h1="About Bodies in Motion"
  eyebrow="Our story"
>
  <p>
    Bodies in Motion is a local company that started in a 1,000 sq. ft. space on Vista Ave. over 20 years ago, as a
    martial art school whose purpose was to Ignite Activity and Encourage Empowerment. Founders Duncan and Rachel
    Richardson, who are still very active in the company, have taught thousands of students in the Treasure Valley.
    In January of 2011 they closed their martial art school on a Friday and re-opened it as Bodies in Motion on Monday,
    and since opening day we’ve had the pleasure of igniting activity in over 60,000 guests.
  </p>
  <p>
    The name comes from Sir Isaac Newton’s 1st Law of Motion, which Duncan thought of as a metaphor for life: a body in
    motion will stay in motion, until acted upon by an external force. Our culture is centered around 7 Core Values
    (Commitment to Guests, Commitment to Work, Unique &amp; Innovative, Always Learning &amp; Knowing, Camaraderie,
    Motion, and Fun) and our purpose: we are committed to igniting activity and encouraging empowerment.
  </p>
